<div class="blurb">
<div class="header"><h2>the problem</h2></div>
<div class="body">
<ul>
<li>MSG is widely used in processed foods and quick-service restaurants (QSRs) <sup><a href="#src-qsr-1">qsr-1</a>, <a href="#src-qsr-2">qsr-2</a>, <a href="#src-qsr-3">qsr-3</a>, <a href="#src-qsr-4">qsr-4</a></sup></li>
<li>Restaurants are <strong>not required</strong> to disclose MSG use (trade secret)</li>
<li>Labeling laws don't require quantity disclosure</li>
<li>"No MSG" is impossible &mdash; only "no added MSG" is accurate</li>
<li><strong>Hidden sodium</strong> - MSG and DSG add sodium to diet without disclosure; DSG has 2x the sodium of MSG</li>
<li><strong>MSG + DSG together</strong> - Often used in combination for synergistic effect, amplifying both sodium and glutamate exposure <sup><a href="#src-synergy">synergy</a>, <a href="#src-synergy-2">synergy-2</a>, <a href="#src-synergy-3">synergy-3</a>, <a href="#src-synergy-4">synergy-4</a></sup></li>
<li>People on low-sodium diets may unknowingly exceed their daily limit</li>
<li><strong>MSG Symptom Complex</strong> (formerly "Chinese Restaurant Syndrome") - controversial but documented reactions in sensitive individuals <sup><a href="#src-symptoms">symptoms</a>, <a href="#src-symptoms-2">symptoms-2</a>, <a href="#src-symptoms-3">symptoms-3</a>, <a href="#src-symptoms-4">symptoms-4</a></sup></li>
<li><strong>Big snack brands admit it</strong> - Frito-Lay: "In order to maintain the taste that consumers have grown to love... we use extremely low levels of MSG in some products to enhance flavor" <sup><a href="#src-frito">frito</a>, <a href="#src-frito-2">frito-2</a>, <a href="#src-frito-3">frito-3</a>, <a href="#src-frito-4">frito-4</a></sup></li>
<li><strong>Skin contact</strong> - Avoid food with MSG on cracked/chapped lips; may sting like salt on a wound <sup><a href="#src-skin">skin</a>, <a href="#src-skin-2">skin-2</a></sup></li>
<li><strong>Military normalization</strong> - U.S. military has used MSG in rations since the Korean War (1950s). Modern MREs use <strong>Disodium Guanylate (DSG)</strong> in synergy with hidden glutamate sources (autolyzed yeast, hydrolyzed protein) to achieve the same umami effect <sup><a href="#src-military">military</a>, <a href="#src-military-2">military-2</a>, <a href="#src-military-3">military-3</a>, <a href="#src-military-4">military-4</a></sup></li>
<li><strong>Treating symptoms, not cause</strong> - People use water pills, pain relievers, antacids, etc. to treat MSG effects rather than avoiding MSG. This adds another layer of pharmaceutical burden to the body.</li>
</ul>
</div>
